! Read by SOCA applications only, after MOM_override. The forecast never sees
! this file, and that asymmetry is the whole point of it existing separately.
!
! THIS IS A WORKAROUND. Delete it when SOCA's MOM6 is rebuilt with symmetric
! memory, and delete the file rather than emptying it.
!
! SOCA links its own MOM6 from NOAA-EMC and that copy is built without
! SYMMETRIC_MEMORY_. MOM6 refuses to configure Flather open boundaries in a
! non-symmetric build:
!
!     FATAL: MOM_open_boundary, open_boundary_config:
!            Symmetric memory must be used when using Flather OBCs.
!
! which aborts inside `soca_geom_init`, so on a regional domain with Flather
! boundaries *every* SOCA application dies during geometry construction, before
! it has read an observation or a background. The forecast model is built
! symmetric and runs the same boundaries without complaint, so this is a
! property of the two builds disagreeing and not of the configuration.
!
! Turning the segments off for SOCA is safe for what SOCA actually uses the
! geometry for. It wants longitude, latitude, depth, layer thickness and the
! land mask, and none of those depend on how the boundary is forced: the grid
! with three Flather segments and the grid with none are the same grid. What is
! lost is MOM6's own knowledge that those columns are boundary columns, which
! matters for the eventual masking of the analysis at the grid edge. That has to
! be handled explicitly regardless (see Domains in docs/design.md, grid edge
! masking) and it is not handled by this.
!
! The real fix is a build-level decision, recorded as a TODO in soca-science
! years ago and still open: build SOCA's MOM6 with symmetric memory so that both
! halves of the system agree about array shapes. Until then this file, and the
! restart-shape conversion its absence used to require, are the cost.

#override OBC_NUMBER_OF_SEGMENTS = 0
